          "Under Section 46, an importer must elect one of three distinct statutory Bill of Entry classifications depending on their immediate supply chain and treasury strategy. The first is the Bill of Entry for Home Consumption (Form I - White BOE). This classification is selected when the importer intends to clear the goods immediately into the domestic economy by paying applicable Basic Customs Duty (BCD), Social Welfare Surcharge (SWS), and Integrated GST (IGST) under Section 47. Upon payment of duties and completion of physical or non-intrusive container scanning, the proper officer issues an Out of Charge (OOC) order under Section 47, permitting the cargo to leave the port terminal.",
