          "To eliminate compliance ambiguity and automate customs appraisal audits across high-volume import operations, enterprise architecture requires an algorithmic classification and valuation engine. The Python class implemented below, CustomsClassificationValuationEngine, operationalizes the six General Rules of Interpretation (GRI) alongside the mandatory Rule 10 additions of the Customs Valuation Rules, 2007.",
          "The engine structures the classification decision logic sequentially. It first evaluates GRI 1 criteria by matching tariff heading descriptions and verifying statutory chapter exclusions. If a multi-component article or retail set is identified, the engine applies GRI 3(b) by calculating the quantitative essential character score\u2014derived from the weighted aggregate of component cost, functional weight, and primary operational utility. If competing headings share identical essential character scores, the engine programmatically triggers the GRI 3(c) statutory tie-breaker, selecting the four-digit heading that appears last in numerical order within the First Schedule.",
          "On the valuation dimension, the engine takes the commercial invoice Free on Board (FOB) price and applies the statutory adjustments mandated by Rule 10. It scrutinizes commission line items, ensuring that selling commissions are added while buying commissions are strictly excluded. It incorporates engineering and design assists performed outside India while isolating domestic engineering work. For transportation, the engine verifies whether ocean or air freight is specified; for air cargo, it automatically caps the freight component at exactly twenty percent of the adjusted FOB value in compliance with the proviso to Rule 10(2). If marine insurance documentation is absent, it computes the statutory insurance factor at exactly 1.125 percent of the FOB value.",
          "Once the final Assessable Value (AV) is established in Indian Rupees at the CBIC notified foreign exchange rate, the engine computes the full customs duty schedule: Basic Customs Duty (BCD) at the applicable tariff rate, Social Welfare Surcharge (SWS) at ten percent of BCD, and Integrated GST (IGST) under Section 3(7) of the Customs Tariff Act on the aggregate of AV plus BCD plus SWS. Rounding rules under Section 154B are applied at each tax component boundary.",
