          "Simultaneously, the exporter must maintain their Average Export Obligation (AEO). The Average Export Obligation represents the historical arithmetic mean of physical exports achieved by the company in the preceding three licensing years for the same or similar products. The statutory rule is uncompromising: the specific export obligation (six times the duty saved) must be fulfilled OVER AND ABOVE the historical average export obligation! Any export revenue realized during the six-year validity period is first allocated to extinguish the baseline Average EO; only the excess export turnover realized beyond the Average EO is counted toward the satisfaction of the specific six-times EPCG export obligation.",
